-- gab/entscheidung.gab -- lane bm9: the per-packet decision wiring.
--
-- This file owns one function the driver calls per packet (`entscheide`),
-- one clock atomic (`UHR_TICK` with its `tick`), one rule-hit lookup
-- (`treffer_index`), and one checker-shaped helper (`zaehle_weiter`). It
-- owns no other table and duplicates none: every foreign name arrives
-- through an `extern fn` mirror -- or, for the connection lock, a `lock`
-- mirror -- with a C-identical prototype (the shape lane bm7 used in
-- gab/lauf.gab; see messung/BEFUNDE-bm7.md L-4). The composition of the
-- eight units happens in C: each module emits its own translation unit and
-- one `cc` link resolves the mirrors. No carrier is defined twice (each
-- definition stands exactly once, in its owner), so the split-brain warning
-- of messung/BEFUNDE-bm8.md (per-file emit duplicating shared carriers)
-- does not apply to this construction.
--
-- MIRROR HONESTY, stated once. The mirrors carry the TRUE effects of their
-- owners (copied from the defining signatures, not `pure`): what the
-- footprints below say is what the owners do, and the caller's coverage is
-- checked against it -- no E009 fires (an `extern` target is known to the
-- graph, same as in gab/lauf.gab). What the checker cannot do from one file
-- is CONFIRM the footprint: a mirror's effects are a claim about another
-- file, refutable only at the C prototype diff and the link (both measured
-- in BERICHT-bm9.md), not by proof. That is the documented price of the
-- pattern, same as BEFUNDE-bm7.md L-4. Three weakenings vs the owner signatures, all
-- three C-neutral, all three stated:
-- * `passt`'s `index into Regel` travels as plain `u32` (`index into T`
--   lowers to `uint32_t` -- BEFUNDE-bm7.md L-4). The Gabbro-side proof that
--   the slot is in range is lost at the mirror; the C is identical, and the
--   only caller (`treffer_index`) guards `k < 256` before every call.
-- * `VSPERRE` is re-declared here (`pub lock ... rank 0 held <= 1024 ops`,
--   same name, rank and bound as gab/verbindungen.gab). The declaration is
--   checker scaffolding: it emits the same `VSPERRE_nimm/gib` calls the
--   owner's side emits, and the link provides the single definition (a
--   pthread mutex in the test harness; the shipped runtime is treiber-lane
--   work). If the owner's rank or bound ever changes, this line follows it.
-- * `suche_oder_lege_an`'s mirror repeats `requires Held(VSPERRE)`; the call
--   stands inside `locks VSPERRE`, so the set is exact (SG-20).
--
-- COSTS. A `costs` promise over an `extern` body is refused (K003 -- part of
-- the 25-error lone-file gate of lane bm8, messung/BEFUNDE-bm8.md F1). Like
-- gab/lauf.gab, this file therefore promises costs only where the body is
-- local (`tick`, measured 10 ops, slack 0); every caller of a mirror
-- carries no `costs` line. `gabbro kosten` reports those sites OFFEN, and
-- the 91166-ops worst case of lane bm8 stands in BERICHT-bm8.md as the last
-- composed measurement, not as a promise.
--
-- THE POLICY, in wire order. The order below IS the firewall's policy:
--   1. decode (`entpacke`); a malformed packet is counted (`zaehle_fehl`
--      AND `zaehle_urteil(DROP)`, so GESAMT still counts every packet) and
--      DROPped. No rule is consulted for a packet we could not read.
--   2. read the tuple through the Kopf accessors (lane bm9, gab/pakete.gab)
--      and compute the flow direction -- the local half of the ARCHITEKTUR.md
--      key rule (smaller (address, port) first). It MUST match
--      `suche_oder_lege_an` line for line; if that canonicalization ever
--      changes, this gate follows it.
--   3. look the flow up (`suche_oder_lege_an`) with the decoded tuple and
--      the current time, under `VSPERRE` -- the only statements inside the
--      `locks` block are the lookup and its assignment, so the critical
--      section is exactly one table operation.
--   4. fast path, REPAIRED (lane bm8 F5 -- see below): ACCEPT without
--      walking the rules only for a FORWARD packet answering ESTABLISHED.
--   5. otherwise walk the rules (`entscheide_regeln`); the default policy
--      (`STANDARD`, DROP -- owned by regeln.gab, not repeated here)
--      decides when nothing matches. A refused lookup (state 0: the
--      bucket was full) also lands here -- fail closed -- after surfacing
--      the event through `zaehle_voll`.
--   6. count the verdict (`zaehle_urteil`, exactly once per call, so
--      GESAMT == VERWORFEN + AKZEPTIERT + ABGEWIESEN holds by construction)
--      and, when a rule matched, the rule hit (`zaehle_regel`).
--
-- THE F5 REPAIR, in one paragraph. `suche_oder_lege_an` answers the
-- POST-transition state, so the packet promoting NEW -> ESTABLISHED answers
-- 2 and the old fast path (`zustand == BESTEHEND` -> ACCEPT) let that very
-- packet skip the rules. The repair reads the direction the lookup itself
-- used: a forward-direction packet answering ESTABLISHED was ESTABLISHED
-- before this packet (a forward hit on NEW answers 1, a fresh entry answers
-- 1 -- read `treffer_pflegen` in gab/verbindungen.gab), so only that shape
-- takes the fast path. A reverse packet answering 2 may be the promotion
-- itself and always walks the rules. Price, stated: reverse traffic on an
-- established flow pays a rule walk (fail-closed direction); the promotion
-- side effect itself (a DROPPed packet still moves the table) is NOT undone
-- here -- undoing it wants a verdict-gated lookup, i.e. a verbindungen.gab
-- signature change, which is another lane's file (see BERICHT-bm9.md).
--
-- WHAT THIS FILE STILL CANNOT DO (each with its reason in
-- messung/BEFUNDE-bm9.md unless named here):
-- * wall-clock `jetzt` (packet-count clock -- bm8 F3, kept);
-- * per-thread Kopf/Paket (`faden` guarded, unused -- bm8 F4, kept);
-- * one-walk rule counting (second walk -- bm8 F6, kept, now as a counted
--   `forever` loop: `traverse` over the rule table emits uncompilable C
--   against an unknown table -- BEFUNDE-bm9.md B-2);
-- * count-then-return as two lines (M147 across true-effect calls keeps the
--   `zaehle_weiter` shape -- bm8 F2, kept).
--
-- Verdicts after ARCHITEKTUR.md, connection states after verbindungen.gab
-- (0 frei, 1 NEU, 2 BESTEHEND, 3 SCHLIESSEND), KEIN_TREFFER marks "no rule
-- matched -- the default policy decided" for the counters.

module brandmauer::entscheidung {

-- pakete.gab mirrors (lane bm9 accessors, gab/pakete.gab). Only the six
-- fields the decision reads; `gueltig` arrives as `entpacke`'s answer and
-- `laenge` never reaches the verdict. Ranges repeat the Kopf declaration.
extern fn entpacke(laenge : u32 in 0 .. 1600) -> u32 in 0 .. 1
    effects { reads Paket.slots, writes Kopf.slots };
extern fn gib_kopf_proto() -> u32 in 0 .. 255
    effects { reads Kopf, reads Kopf.slots };
extern fn gib_kopf_quelle() -> u32
    effects { reads Kopf, reads Kopf.slots };
extern fn gib_kopf_ziel() -> u32
    effects { reads Kopf, reads Kopf.slots };
extern fn gib_kopf_qport() -> u32 in 0 .. 65535
    effects { reads Kopf, reads Kopf.slots };
extern fn gib_kopf_zport() -> u32 in 0 .. 65535
    effects { reads Kopf, reads Kopf.slots };
extern fn gib_kopf_flaggen() -> u32 in 0 .. 255
    effects { reads Kopf, reads Kopf.slots };

-- regeln.gab mirrors. `r` travels as plain `u32` (see the file head):
-- the C is `uint32_t`, the Gabbro index proof is the caller's guard.
extern fn passt(r : u32, proto : u32 in 0 .. 255, quelle : u32, ziel : u32, qport : u32 in 0 .. 65535, zport : u32 in 0 .. 65535, flaggen : u32 in 0 .. 255) -> u32 in 0 .. 1
    effects { reads Regel, reads Regel.slots };
extern fn entscheide_regeln(proto : u32 in 0 .. 255, quelle : u32, ziel : u32, qport : u32 in 0 .. 65535, zport : u32 in 0 .. 65535, flaggen : u32 in 0 .. 255) -> u32 in 0 .. 2
    effects { reads Regel, reads Regel.slots };

-- verbindungen.gab mirrors. Same name, rank and held bound as the owner;
-- checker scaffolding emitting the same call names (see the file head).
pub lock VSPERRE protects { Verbindung, Stand } rank 0 held <= 1024 ops;

extern fn suche_oder_lege_an(quelle : u32, ziel : u32, qport : u32 in 0 .. 65535, zport : u32 in 0 .. 65535, iprot : u32 in 0 .. 255, flaggen : u32 in 0 .. 255, jetzt : u32) -> u32 in 0 .. 3
    requires Held(VSPERRE)
    effects { reads Verbindung.slots, writes Verbindung.slots, reads Stand.slots, writes Stand.slots, locks VSPERRE };

-- zaehler.gab mirrors. The `zaehle_regel` footprint below is the owner's,
-- entry for entry (256 per-rule atomics plus the sum).
extern fn zaehle_urteil(u : u32 in 0 .. 2)
    effects { reads VERWORFEN, writes VERWORFEN, reads AKZEPTIERT, writes AKZEPTIERT, reads ABGEWIESEN, writes ABGEWIESEN, reads GESAMT, writes GESAMT };
extern fn zaehle_regel(r : u32 in 0 .. 255)
    effects { reads REGEL000, writes REGEL000, reads REGEL001, writes REGEL001, reads REGEL002, writes REGEL002, reads REGEL003, writes REGEL003, reads REGEL004, writes REGEL004, reads REGEL005, writes REGEL005, reads REGEL006, writes REGEL006, reads REGEL007, writes REGEL007, reads REGEL008, writes REGEL008, reads REGEL009, writes REGEL009, reads REGEL010, writes REGEL010, reads REGEL011, writes REGEL011, reads REGEL012, writes REGEL012, reads REGEL013, writes REGEL013, reads REGEL014, writes REGEL014, reads REGEL015, writes REGEL015, reads REGEL016, writes REGEL016, reads REGEL017, writes REGEL017, reads REGEL018, writes REGEL018, reads REGEL019, writes REGEL019, reads REGEL020, writes REGEL020, reads REGEL021, writes REGEL021, reads REGEL022, writes REGEL022, reads REGEL023, writes REGEL023, reads REGEL024, writes REGEL024, reads REGEL025, writes REGEL025, reads REGEL026, writes REGEL026, reads REGEL027, writes REGEL027, reads REGEL028, writes REGEL028, reads REGEL029, writes REGEL029, reads REGEL030, writes REGEL030, reads REGEL031, writes REGEL031, reads REGEL032, writes REGEL032, reads REGEL033, writes REGEL033, reads REGEL034, writes REGEL034, reads REGEL035, writes REGEL035, reads REGEL036, writes REGEL036, reads REGEL037, writes REGEL037, reads REGEL038, writes REGEL038, reads REGEL039, writes REGEL039, reads REGEL040, writes REGEL040, reads REGEL041, writes REGEL041, reads REGEL042, writes REGEL042, reads REGEL043, writes REGEL043, reads REGEL044, writes REGEL044, reads REGEL045, writes REGEL045, reads REGEL046, writes REGEL046, reads REGEL047, writes REGEL047, reads REGEL048, writes REGEL048, reads REGEL049, writes REGEL049, reads REGEL050, writes REGEL050, reads REGEL051, writes REGEL051, reads REGEL052, writes REGEL052, reads REGEL053, writes REGEL053, reads REGEL054, writes REGEL054, reads REGEL055, writes REGEL055, reads REGEL056, writes REGEL056, reads REGEL057, writes REGEL057, reads REGEL058, writes REGEL058, reads REGEL059, writes REGEL059, reads REGEL060, writes REGEL060, reads REGEL061, writes REGEL061, reads REGEL062, writes REGEL062, reads REGEL063, writes REGEL063, reads REGEL064, writes REGEL064, reads REGEL065, writes REGEL065, reads REGEL066, writes REGEL066, reads REGEL067, writes REGEL067, reads REGEL068, writes REGEL068, reads REGEL069, writes REGEL069, reads REGEL070, writes REGEL070, reads REGEL071, writes REGEL071, reads REGEL072, writes REGEL072, reads REGEL073, writes REGEL073, reads REGEL074, writes REGEL074, reads REGEL075, writes REGEL075, reads REGEL076, writes REGEL076, reads REGEL077, writes REGEL077, reads REGEL078, writes REGEL078, reads REGEL079, writes REGEL079, reads REGEL080, writes REGEL080, reads REGEL081, writes REGEL081, reads REGEL082, writes REGEL082, reads REGEL083, writes REGEL083, reads REGEL084, writes REGEL084, reads REGEL085, writes REGEL085, reads REGEL086, writes REGEL086, reads REGEL087, writes REGEL087, reads REGEL088, writes REGEL088, reads REGEL089, writes REGEL089, reads REGEL090, writes REGEL090, reads REGEL091, writes REGEL091, reads REGEL092, writes REGEL092, reads REGEL093, writes REGEL093, reads REGEL094, writes REGEL094, reads REGEL095, writes REGEL095, reads REGEL096, writes REGEL096, reads REGEL097, writes REGEL097, reads REGEL098, writes REGEL098, reads REGEL099, writes REGEL099, reads REGEL100, writes REGEL100, reads REGEL101, writes REGEL101, reads REGEL102, writes REGEL102, reads REGEL103, writes REGEL103, reads REGEL104, writes REGEL104, reads REGEL105, writes REGEL105, reads REGEL106, writes REGEL106, reads REGEL107, writes REGEL107, reads REGEL108, writes REGEL108, reads REGEL109, writes REGEL109, reads REGEL110, writes REGEL110, reads REGEL111, writes REGEL111, reads REGEL112, writes REGEL112, reads REGEL113, writes REGEL113, reads REGEL114, writes REGEL114, reads REGEL115, writes REGEL115, reads REGEL116, writes REGEL116, reads REGEL117, writes REGEL117, reads REGEL118, writes REGEL118, reads REGEL119, writes REGEL119, reads REGEL120, writes REG